ants.\r\naudit/findings/F-017.md:45:The API accepts arbitrary `OrderStatus` enum values from the client payload during order creation. A salesman can directly create orders with `status: \"APPROVED\"`, completely bypassing manager authorization, ATP stock checks, credit limit checks, and stock reservation creation. The order exists in the database as `APPROVED` with 0 stock reserved, corrupting downstream fulfilment invariants.\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius-f011.sh:12:echo \"--- 2. Running Invariants Check (10 SQL invariants) ---\"\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius-f011.sh:13:PGPASSWORD=postgres psql -U postgres -h localhost -d mill_ledger -f audit/scripts/invariants.sql\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius-cluster02.sh:13:  echo \"--- 2. Running SQL Database Invariants (10 invariants) ---\"\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius-cluster02.sh:14:  PGPASSWORD=postgres psql -U postgres -h localhost -d mill_ledger -f audit/scripts/invariants.sql\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius-f097.sh:16:PGPASSWORD=postgres psql -U postgres -h localhost -d mill_ledger -f audit/scripts/invariants.sql\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius.sh:12:echo \"--- 2. Running Invariants Check (10 SQL invariants) ---\"\r\naudit/scripts/verify/07-regression-radius.sh:13:PGPASSWORD=postgres psql -U postgres -h localhost -d mill_ledger -f audit/scripts/invariants.sql\r\naudit/scripts/verify-domain-validation.ts:253:    expectedBehavior: \"Enforce chronological invariants (dueDate \u003e= invoiceDate, paymentDate \u003c= current_date)\",\r\naudit/scripts/invariants.sql:3:-- Execute against PostgreSQL: psql -f invariants.sql\r\naudit/evidence/semgrep-results.json:1:{\"version\":\"1.186.0\",\"results\":[{\"check_id\":\"yaml.github-actions.security.github-actions-mutable-action-tag.github-actions-mutable-action-tag\",\"path\":\".github/workflows/ci.yml\",\"start\":{\"line\":43,\"col\":9,\"offset\":1018},\"end\":{\"line\":43,\"col\":34,\"offset\":